{"title": "Ratio and Proportion (Level 2)", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>An item is a mixture of three metals gold, silver and copper. Its weight is 500gm. ratio of weight of metals are in the ratio 2:3:5. Given that the price is directly proportional to the square of weight of that metal, then find the price of other metals if the price of gold is Rs 500 per gram.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;, &#2330;&#2366;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 500 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 2:3:5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2313;&#2360; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; 500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p>", "options_en": ["Rs 112500 and Rs 312500", "Rs 100000 and Rs 200000", "Rs 99500 and Rs 112500", "Rs 125000 and Rs 135000"], "options_hi": ["112500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 312500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "100000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 200000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "99500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 112500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "125000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 135000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The price is directly proportional to the square of weight of that metal,</p><p>Therefore price = kw<sup>2</sup> (k is a constant)</p><p>Weight of gold = 2/(2+3+5) x 500 = 100g</p><p>Price of gold is Rs 500 per gram, therefore</p><p>500 x 100 = k x 100 x 100</p><p>=&gt; k = 5</p><p>Price of silver = 5 x 150 x 150 = 112500</p><p>Price of copper = 5 x 250 x 250 = 312500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The price is directly proportional to the square of weight of that metal,</p><p>Therefore price = kw<sup>2</sup> (k is a constant)</p><p>Weight of gold = 2/(2+3+5) x 500 = 100g</p><p>Price of gold is Rs 500 per gram, therefore</p><p>500 x 100 = k x 100 x 100</p><p>=&gt; k = 5</p><p>Price of silver = 5 x 150 x 150 = 112500</p><p>Price of copper = 5 x 250 x 250 = 312500</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 561: 11:: 510: x and y: 266 :: 42: 228, then find (2x + y).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 561: 11:: 510: x &#2324;&#2352; y: 266 :: 42: 228 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (2x + y) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["54", "69", "72", "81"], "options_hi": ["54", "69", "72", "81"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Here, 561: 11:: 510: x</p><p>x = 510 * 11/561 = 10</p><p>And, y: 266 :: 42: 228</p><p>y = 266 * 42/228 = 49</p><p>Therefore, 2x + y = 2 * 10 + 49 = <b>69</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, 561: 11:: 510: x</p><p>x = 510 * 11/561 = 10</p><p>And, y: 266 :: 42: 228</p><p>y = 266 * 42/228 = 49</p><p>Therefore, 2x + y = 2 * 10 + 49 = <b>69</b></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are three metals named as A, B, and C. The ratio of weight of metal A to that of metal C is 25: 1 and the ratio of weight of metal B to that of C is 17: 1. In what ratio metals A and B be mixed so that the ratio of weight of mixture to weight of metal C is 19: 1?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B, &#2324;&#2352; C &#2344;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 25: 1 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 17:1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2325;&#2367; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 19:1 &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["3: 2", "1: 2", "2: 3", "1: 3"], "options_hi": ["3: 2", "1: 2", "2: 3", "1: 3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p>The ratio of weight of metal A to that of metal C is 25: 1.</p><p>Therefore, metal A is 25 times as heavy as metal C.</p><p>Similarly, metal B is 17 times as heavy as metal C.</p><p>Required ratio = (19  -  17)/ (25  -  19) = 2/6 = 1: 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p>The ratio of weight of metal A to that of metal C is 25: 1.</p><p>Therefore, metal A is 25 times as heavy as metal C.</p><p>Similarly, metal B is 17 times as heavy as metal C.</p><p>Required ratio = (19  -  17)/ (25  -  19) = 2/6 = 1: 3</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 25% of A is equal to 40% of B, then (A + B) : (A &#8211; B) is equal to :&nbsp;</span></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2325;&#2366; 25%, B &#2325;&#2375; 40% &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (A + B) : (A - B) &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7: 4", "7: 3", "13: 8", "13: 3"], "options_hi": ["7: 4", "7: 3", "13: 8", "13: 3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>A/4 = (2/5) of B</p><p>A/B = 8/5</p><p>Let A = 8 and B = 5</p><p>A + B = 13</p><p>A - B = 3</p><p>Required ratio = 13: 3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>A/4 = (2/5) of B</p><p>A/B = 8/5</p><p>Let A = 8 and B = 5</p><p>A + B = 13</p><p>A - B = 3</p><p>Required ratio = 13: 3</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The respective ratio of the initial number of notebooks A has to that of B has, is 2: 3. And the respective ratio of the number of notebooks sold by A to that of by B is 3: 4. If the number of notebooks sold by B is 80% of the number of initial notebooks A has, then find the ratio of the number of notebooks left with A to that of with B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; B &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, A &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 80% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4: 7", "5: 3", "3: 7", "7: 5"], "options_hi": ["4: 7", "5: 3", "3: 7", "7: 5"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let initial number of notebooks A has = 2X</p><p>And initial number of notebooks B has = 3X</p><p>And number of notebooks sold by A = 3Y</p><p>And number of notebooks sold by B = 4Y</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>4Y = 2X *4/5</p><p>5Y = 2X</p><p>Number of notebooks left with A = 2X  -  3Y = 5Y  -  3Y = 2Y</p><p>Number of notebooks left with B = 3X  -  4Y = (15Y/2)  -  4Y = 7Y/2</p><p>Required ratio = 2Y: (7Y/2) = 4: 7.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let initial number of notebooks A has = 2X</p><p>And initial number of notebooks B has = 3X</p><p>And number of notebooks sold by A = 3Y</p><p>And number of notebooks sold by B = 4Y</p><p>ATQ,</p><p>4Y = 2X *4/5</p><p>5Y = 2X</p><p>Number of notebooks left with A = 2X  -  3Y = 5Y  -  3Y = 2Y</p><p>Number of notebooks left with B = 3X  -  4Y = (15Y/2)  -  4Y = 7Y/2</p><p>Required ratio = 2Y: (7Y/2) = 4: 7.</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number of marbles in three jars are in the ratio of 6: 7: 9. If 30, 50, and 80 more marbles are put in the jars, respectively, the new ratio becomes 9: 12: 17. The new total number of marbles in the jars is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 6: 7: 9 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 30, 50 &#2324;&#2352; 80 &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2306;&#2330;&#2375; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 9: 12: 17 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2306;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2312; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["350", "360", "380", "400"], "options_hi": ["350", "360", "380", "400"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>New ratio = 9: 12: 17</p><p>Sum of new ratio = 38</p><p>So, the answer will be a multiple of 38, hence 380 will be the answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>New ratio = 9: 12: 17</p><p>Sum of new ratio = 38</p><p>So, the answer will be a multiple of 38, hence 380 will be the answer.</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If third proportion of 102, and x is 408, then what is the value of x?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 102 &#2324;&#2352; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2371;&#2340;&#2368;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; 408 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["102", "204", "68", "170"], "options_hi": ["102", "204", "68", "170"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given, third proportion of 102, and x is 408.</p><p>=&gt; 408 = (x * x)/102</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> = 408 * 102</p><p>=&gt; x = 204</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given, third proportion of 102, and x is 408.</p><p>=&gt; 408 = (x * x)/102</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> = 408 * 102</p><p>=&gt; x = 204</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are three integers x, y and z such that the ratio of sum of value of x and y to sum of values of y and z is 8: 9 and the ratio of value of y and z is 5: 2, then find the ratio of the value of x to the value of z?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; x, y &#2324;&#2352; z &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; y &#2324;&#2352; z &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 8:9 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; y &#2324;&#2352; z &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 5:2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; z &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["9: 11", "11: 20", "11: 18", "13: 21"], "options_hi": ["9: 11", "11: 20", "11: 18", "13: 21"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the value of y = 5a and the value of z = 2a</p><p>So, (x + y)/(y + z) = 8/9</p><p>=&gt; (x + 5a)/(5a + 2a) = 8/9</p><p>=&gt; 9x + 45a = 56a</p><p>=&gt; 9x = 11a</p><p>=&gt; x = 11a/9</p><p>Hence, required ratio = 11a/9: 2a = 11: 18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the value of y = 5a and the value of z = 2a</p><p>So, (x + y)/(y + z) = 8/9</p><p>=&gt; (x + 5a)/(5a + 2a) = 8/9</p><p>=&gt; 9x + 45a = 56a</p><p>=&gt; 9x = 11a</p><p>=&gt; x = 11a/9</p><p>Hence, required ratio = 11a/9: 2a = 11: 18</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>X is inversely proportional to Y and inversely proportional to square of Z. When Y = 10 and Z = 4, then X = 12. What will be the value of Z when X = 16, and Y = 3?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X, Y &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; Z &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Y = 10 &#2324;&#2352; Z = 4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X = 12 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = 16 &#2324;&#2352; Y = 3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Z &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;10", "2&radic;10", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5"], "options_hi": ["&radic;10", "2&radic;10", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=39 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=56 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=59 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=84 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=39 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=56 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=65 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p22970/image008.png\"></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The compound ratio of 6: 13 and 10:14 is X: 26. Find X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>6: 13 &#2324;&#2352; 10:14 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; X: 26 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8", "60/7", "9", "52/7"], "options_hi": ["8", "60/7", "9", "52/7"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(6/13) * (10/14) = X/26</p><p>X = 60/7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to question,</p><p>(6/13) * (10/14) = X/26</p><p>X = 60/7</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>What number is subtracted from each of 20, 24, 32 and 40, such that all are in proportion in same order?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>20, 24, 32 &#2324;&#2352; 40 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2320;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;?</p>", "options_en": ["4", "6", "8", "10"], "options_hi": ["4", "6", "8", "10"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number subtracted = n</p><p>Then, (20  -  n): (24  -  n) :: (32  -  n): (40  -  n)</p><p>(20  -  n)(40  -  n) = (32  -  n)(24  -  n)</p><p>800  -  60n + n<sup>2</sup> = 768  -  56n + n<sup>2</sup></p><p>4n = 32</p><p><b>n = 8</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number subtracted = n</p><p>Then, (20  -  n): (24  -  n) :: (32  -  n): (40  -  n)</p><p>(20  -  n)(40  -  n) = (32  -  n)(24  -  n)</p><p>800  -  60n + n<sup>2</sup> = 768  -  56n + n<sup>2</sup></p><p>4n = 32</p><p><b>n = 8</b></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The expenditure and savings of Sachin are in the ratio of 7:4 respectively and the income of Manish and Sachin are in the ratio of 5:7 respectively. If the income of Manish is &#8377;13750, then find the savings of Sachin.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2330;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 7 : 4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2350;&#2344;&#2368;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2330;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 : 7 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2344;&#2368;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#8377;13750 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2330;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2330;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;7000", "&#8377;8600", "&#8377;6000", "&#8377;9600"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;7000", "&#8377;8600", "&#8377;6000", "&#8377;9600"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Income of Manish = &#8377;13750</p><p>Income of Sachin = (7/5) * 13750 = &#8377;19250</p><p>Savings of Sachin = (4/11) * 19250 = &#8377;7000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Income of Manish = &#8377;13750</p><p>Income of Sachin = (7/5) * 13750 = &#8377;19250</p><p>Savings of Sachin = (4/11) * 19250 = &#8377;7000</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A number 405 is divided into three parts in the ratio 4: 2: 3 respectively. The three parts are:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 405 &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:2:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2305;&#2335;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["180, 90 and 135", "160, 90 and 155", "160, 100 and 145", "200, 70 and 135"], "options_hi": ["180, 90 &#2324;&#2352; 135", "160, 90 &#2324;&#2352; 155", "160, 100 &#2324;&#2352; 145", "200, 70 &#2324;&#2352; 135"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>First part = 405 * 4/9 = 180</p><p>Second part = 405 * 2/9 = 90</p><p>Third part = 405 * 3/9 = 135</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>First part = 405 * 4/9 = 180</p><p>Second part = 405 * 2/9 = 90</p><p>Third part = 405 * 3/9 = 135</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A is inversely proportional to B and inversely proportional to square of C. When B = 20 and C = 2&radic;2, then A = 24. What will be the value of C when A = 32, and B = 9?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; B = 20 &#2324;&#2352; C = 2&radic;2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A = 24 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 32 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B = 9 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["&radic;10/3", "2&radic;(10/3)", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5/3"], "options_hi": ["&radic;10/3", "2&radic;(10/3)", "2&radic;5", "&radic;5/3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image003.png\"></p><p>K=3840</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=61 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image003.png\"></p><p>K=3840</p><p>Now,</p><p><img width=77 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=57 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23931/image006.png\"></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If fourth proportional of (x + 11), 30 and (3x  -  9) is 45, then find the value of x.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (x + 11), 30 &#2324;&#2352; (3x - 9) &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; 45 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["17", "18", "15", "13"], "options_hi": ["17", "18", "15", "13"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Here, (x + 11): 30:: (3x  -  9): 45</p><p>(x + 11) * 45 = (3x  -  9) * 30</p><p>(x + 11) = (x  -  3) * 2</p><p>x + 11 = 2x  -  6</p><p>x = 17</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, (x + 11): 30:: (3x  -  9): 45</p><p>(x + 11) * 45 = (3x  -  9) * 30</p><p>(x + 11) = (x  -  3) * 2</p><p>x + 11 = 2x  -  6</p><p>x = 17</p><p></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two numbers are such that their difference, their sum, and their product are to one another as 1 : 7 : 24. The product of the two numbers is :</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;, &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2398;&#2354; 1:7:24 &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;| &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["6", "12", "24", "48"], "options_hi": ["6", "12", "24", "48"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers be a and b</p> \n<p>a - b = x</p> \n<p>a + b = 7x</p> \n<p>ab = 24x </p> \n<p>Solving the first two equations, we get: </p> \n<p>a = 4x and b = 3x</p> \n<p>Substituting these values in the third, we get x = 2.</p> \n<p>Now, product is,</p> \n<p>ab = 24 * 2 = 48</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers be a and b</p> \n<p>a - b = x</p> \n<p>a + b = 7x</p> \n<p>ab = 24x </p> \n<p>Solving the first two equations, we get: </p> \n<p>a = 4x and b = 3x</p> \n<p>Substituting these values in the third, we get x = 2.</p> \n<p>Now, product is,</p> \n<p>ab = 24 * 2 = 48</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a map 3/7 cm represents 24 km. If two cities are 13/4 cm apart on the map, what is the actual distance between them?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 3/7 cm, 24 km &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; 13/4 cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["182 km", "185 km", "188 km", "190 km"], "options_hi": ["182 km", "185 km", "188 km", "190 km"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>In a map 3/7 cm represents 24 km</p><p>According to question,</p><p>3/7 = 24</p><p>1 = 56</p><p>13/4 = 56 * 13/4 = 182 km</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In a map 3/7 cm represents 24 km</p><p>According to question,</p><p>3/7 = 24</p><p>1 = 56</p><p>13/4 = 56 * 13/4 = 182 km</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of two numbers A and B is 5 : 8 respectively. If 5 is added to each of A and B, then the ratio becomes 2 : 3 respectively. The difference between A and B is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5 : 8 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2332;&#2379;&#2396;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2 : 3 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["15", "20", "12", "10"], "options_hi": ["15", "20", "12", "10"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let numbers be 5x and 8x.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(5x + 5)/ (8x + 5) = 2/3</p><p>15x + 15 = 16x + 10</p><p>x = 5</p><p>Required difference = 8x - 5x = 3x = 15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let numbers be 5x and 8x.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(5x + 5)/ (8x + 5) = 2/3</p><p>15x + 15 = 16x + 10</p><p>x = 5</p><p>Required difference = 8x - 5x = 3x = 15</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>When 'p' is added to each of the numbers 76, 67, 22 and 19, the numbers so obtained are in proportion, then ratio of (7p  -  10): (6p + 5) will be ?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; 76, 67, 22 &#2324;&#2352; 19 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 'p' &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, (7p - 10): (6p + 5) &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7: 5", "4: 5", "5: 7", "3: 4"], "options_hi": ["7: 5", "4: 5", "5: 7", "3: 4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>(76+p): (67+p) :: (22+p) : (19+p)</p><p><img width=107 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15551/image004.png\"></p><p>76 X 19 + 76p + 19p + p<sup>2</sup> = 67 X 22 + 67p + 22p + p<sup>2</sup></p><p>1444 + 95p = 1474 + 89p</p><p>6p = 30</p><p>p = 5</p><p>(7p  -  10) = 35  -  10 = 25</p><p>(6p + 5) = 30 + 5 = 35</p><p>Required ratio = 25: 35 = 5: 7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(76+p): (67+p) :: (22+p) : (19+p)</p><p><img width=107 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p15551/image004.png\"></p><p>76 X 19 + 76p + 19p + p<sup>2</sup> = 67 X 22 + 67p + 22p + p<sup>2</sup></p><p>1444 + 95p = 1474 + 89p</p><p>6p = 30</p><p>p = 5</p><p>(7p  -  10) = 35  -  10 = 25</p><p>(6p + 5) = 30 + 5 = 35</p><p>Required ratio = 25: 35 = 5: 7</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a:b = 3:4, b:c = 2:3, c:d = 1:2, then find the value of ((a + b + c + d)/(b + d))<sup>1/2</sup></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a:b = 3:4, b:c = 2:3, c:d = 1:2, &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; ((a + b + c + d)/(b + d))<sup>1/2 </sup>&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;|</p>", "options_en": ["4:5", "2:3", "5:4", "1:1"], "options_hi": ["4:5", "2:3", "5:4", "1:1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a:b = 3:4</p> <p>b:c = 2:3 = 4:6</p> <p>c:d = 1:2 = 6:12</p> <p>Hence, a:b:c:d = 3:4:6:12</p> <p>Required value = ((3+4+6+12)/(4+12)) <sup>1/2 </sup>= 5/4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a:b = 3:4</p> <p>b:c = 2:3 = 4:6</p> <p>c:d = 1:2 = 6:12</p> <p>Hence, a:b:c:d = 3:4:6:12</p> <p>Required value = ((3+4+6+12)/(4+12)) <sup>1/2 </sup>= 5/4</p>"}]}